ingle team would go on to win at least one game in the round-robin of the tournament, including a dramatic shootout win for the host country, China over Japan. The medal matches ended up as predicted, with the United States and Canada (with a perfect record) advancing to the gold medal game while Finland and Switzerland battled for the bronze. Canada continued their perfect tournament with a 3-2 victory over their rivals with the game-winning goal scored by team captain " [:a {:href "/athletes/119286"} "Marie-Philip Poulin"] ", capturing their fifth gold medal in the event. Poulin also became the first and, to date, only ice hockey player to score in four Olympic gold medal games. In the bronze medal game, Finland won by a decisive 4-0 score over Switzerland, capturing their fourth medal in the event and successfully defending their bronze medal from PyeongChang 2018."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button585913", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button585913').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Assists"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalties in Minutes (PIM)"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Plus/Minus"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Saves"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Save%"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals Against Average"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Shots on Goal"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Minutes Played"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "